uina Común","dish/esquina-comun"]]}]},"ingredient/bilberries":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bilberries","n":"Bilberries","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Bilberry (), also known as European blueberry, is a Eurasian low-growing shrub in the genus Vaccinium of the flowering plant family Ericaceae. Vaccinium myrtillus L. is the species most commonly called bilberry, but other closely related Vaccinium species may also have this name."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bilberries"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bilberries"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine",[["Blåbärssoppa","dish/blabarssoppa"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Bilberry","ingredient/bilberry"],["Potato starch","ingredient/potato-starch"],["Starch","ingredient/starch"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/43/Vaccinium_myrtillus_Mustikka_IMG_1100_C-_cropped.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_myrtillus_Mustikka_IMG_1100_C-_cropped.jpg","w":500,"h":433,"by":"Anneli Salo","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaccinium_myrtillus_Mustikka_IMG_1100_C-_cropped.jpg"}},"dish/cream-of-sorrel-soup":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/cream-of-sorrel-soup","n":"Cream of sorrel soup","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Cream of sorrel soup, also known as potage Germiny, crème Germiny, or potage crème d'oseille, is a traditional French springtime vegetable soup, often served cold. It can be made with French sorrel (Rumex scutatus), common sorrel (Rumex acetosa), or  foraged wild greens with similar flavor profiles, such as sheep's sorrel (Rumex acetosella), wood sorrel (Oxalis corniculata, Oxalis albicans), sour grass, young leaves of dock (Rumex crispus, Rumex obtusifolius), and others."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cream-of-sorrel-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_of_sorrel_soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["'t Misverstant","dish/t-misverstant"],["'t Vlasbloemeken","dish/t-vlasbloemeken"],["&moshik","dish/moshik"],["Aan de Poel","dish/aan-de-poel"],["Adrian (restaurant)","dish/adrian-restaurant"],["Adventureland Bazaar","dish/adventureland-bazaar"],["Alain Ducasse at The Dorchester","dish/alain-ducasse-at-the-dorchester"],["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Alex (restaurant)","dish/alex-restaurant"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Arpège (restaurant)","dish/arpege-restaurant"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Atelier Crenn","dish/atelier-crenn"],["Au Coin des Bons Enfants","dish/au-coi